Resonans is published by KlangHaus, the trading name of Asp Productions ApS
(Danish CVR 36708077). The copyright is held by the authors of the work.

That wording is deliberate and it replaced a stronger claim that was measured
untrue. An earlier version of this file said Asp Productions ApS held the
copyright. Under Danish law an employer acquires copyright in software written by
an EMPLOYEE (Ophavsretsloven § 59) — and nobody is employed by the company, so
§ 59 transfers nothing and the rights sit with the individual authors. Measured by
[jura], 2026-09-28.

The rights have not been consolidated in a single holder. Until they are, this file
says who holds the copyright rather than who we would like to hold it, because a
notice cannot be withdrawn from a fork.

That sentence used to name an intended holder. [jura] read this file and removed the
forward-looking half, because the sentence was doing the very thing the
one beside it warns against: an intention cannot be checked, it goes stale by
itself, and it cannot be withdrawn from a fork either. What replaced it is a fact,
and a fact does not break when a company changes. The day the transfer is signed,
the FIRST paragraph changes instead — "the authors of the work" becomes whoever
holds it then — which is a factual update made at the moment it becomes true.
